---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import Stat from '../../components/Stat.astro';
import TeamCard from '../../components/TeamCard.astro';
import CityCard from '../../components/CityCard.astro';
import CTASection from '../../components/CTASection.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro';
import { team, beliefs, company } from '../../data/company';
import { cities } from '../../data/cities';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About Precifarm: built and run by a Kenyan team"
  description="Founded 2024 in Kenya. EPRA-licensed EPC and O&M contractor. No outside investors, six operating cities, one engineering team across the country."
  canonicalPath="/about/"
>
  <Hero
    eyebrow="About"
    headline="Built and run by a Kenyan team that answers when you call."
    subhead="EPRA-licensed EPC and O&M contractor. Headquartered in Nairobi, with resident engineering teams in five more cities."
    primaryCta={{ href: '/contact/', label: 'Talk to us' }}
    secondaryCta={{ href: '/how-we-work/', label: 'How we work' }}
  />

  <!-- Key facts -->
  <section class="bg-paper">
    <div class="container-page py-10 md:py-14">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-6 md:gap-10">
        <Stat value="2025" label="Incorporated" />
        <Stat value="6" label="Cities" />
        <Stat value="100%" label="Built in Kenya" />
        <Stat value="0" label="Outside investors" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What we believe -->
  <section class="bg-white">
    <div class="container-page section">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mb-10 md:mb-12">
        <p class="eyebrow mb-3">What we believe</p>
        <h2 class="text-h2-sm md:text-h1 text-navy-dark">Three things we will not compromise on.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="space-y-5">
        {beliefs.map((belief, i) => (
          <article class="rounded-card border border-hairline bg-white p-6 md:p-8">
            <div class="flex items-start gap-5">
              <span class="text-navy font-bold text-2xl shrink-0 w-10">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
              <div class="flex-1">
                <h3 class="text-h3 text-navy-dark">{belief.title}</h3>
                <p class="mt-3 text-text-mid leading-relaxed">{belief.body}</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Why now: three structural curves -->
  <section class="bg-paper">
    <div class="container-page section">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mb-10 md:mb-12">
        <p class="eyebrow mb-3">Why now</p>
        <h2 class="text-h2-sm md:text-h1 text-navy-dark">Three structural curves crossed in 2024.</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-text-mid leading-relaxed">
          Precifarm exists at this moment because three independent shifts converged. Any one of them would matter on its own. All three together is why we launched.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <article class="rounded-card bg-white p-6 md:p-7">
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline gap-3 sm:gap-6">
            <p class="text-3xl font-bold text-navy shrink-0 w-24">2024</p>
            <div class="flex-1">
              <h3 class="text-h3 text-navy-dark">EV vehicles deployed at scale</h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-text-mid leading-relaxed">
                BasiGo electric buses on Nairobi routes. Roam and Spiro electric motorbikes in fleet service. Ampersand swap stations live. ARC Ride scaling rapidly. The vehicles exist on Kenyan roads today. Distributed high-capacity charging infrastructure does not. Commercial Plus is built directly into that gap.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="rounded-card bg-white p-6 md:p-7">
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline gap-3 sm:gap-6">
            <p class="text-3xl font-bold text-navy shrink-0 w-24">2024</p>
            <div class="flex-1">
              <h3 class="text-h3 text-navy-dark">LFP battery price crossed $100 per kWh</h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-text-mid leading-relaxed">
                Lithium iron phosphate pack prices crossed below the $100/kWh threshold. A 1.5 kWh Starter Pod becomes financeable at KSh 5,472 per month on Lipa Pole Pole. A 1 MWh Commercial Plus block becomes commercially mortgageable. The economics that used to require a grant now run on customer revenue.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="rounded-card bg-white p-6 md:p-7">
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline gap-3 sm:gap-6">
            <p class="text-3xl font-bold text-navy shrink-0 w-24">2024</p>
            <div class="flex-1">
              <h3 class="text-h3 text-navy-dark">Kenya Net Metering Regulations gazetted</h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-text-mid leading-relaxed">
                Together with the National Energy Compact targeting 1.8 GW of wind and solar by 2030, this is the most enabling regulatory environment Kenya's distributed energy sector has seen. EPRA licensing, net-metering rules, and the policy framework around grid interconnection are all aligned at the same moment.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Who we serve (market context) -->
  <section class="bg-white">
    <div class="container-page section">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mb-10 md:mb-12">
        <p class="eyebrow mb-3">Who we serve</p>
        <h2 class="text-h2-sm md:text-h1 text-navy-dark">Every Kenyan household, SME, institution, and EV fleet.</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-text-mid leading-relaxed">
          Four packages mapped to four market segments. KNBS data sets the bottom-up scale; our operating footprint sets the path.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto -mx-5 md:mx-0 px-5 md:px-0">
        <table class="w-full min-w-[640px] border-collapse text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col" class="text-left p-4 font-semibold text-text-muted text-xs uppercase tracking-wider border-b-2 border-navy">Segment</th>
              <th scope="col" class="text-left p-4 font-semibold text-text-muted text-xs uppercase tracking-wider border-b-2 border-navy">Scale</th>
              <th scope="col" class="text-left p-4 font-semibold text-text-muted text-xs uppercase tracking-wider border-b-2 border-navy">Precifarm package</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="bg-row-alt">
              <th scope="row" class="text-left p-4 font-semibold text-navy-dark align-top">Off-grid and grid-unreliable households</th>
              <td class="p-4 text-text-mid align-top">12.1 million households<br /><span class="text-xs text-text-muted">KNBS</span></td>
              <td class="p-4 text-text-mid align-top">Starter and Family</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="bg-white">
              <th scope="row" class="text-left p-4 font-semibold text-navy-dark align-top">Kenyan MSMEs</th>
              <td class="p-4 text-text-mid align-top">1.56 million enterprises<br /><span class="text-xs text-text-muted">KNBS</span></td>
              <td class="p-4 text-text-mid align-top">Family and Commercial</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="bg-row-alt">
              <th scope="row" class="text-left p-4 font-semibold text-navy-dark align-top">Schools, clinics, agricultural cooperatives</th>
              <td class="p-4 text-text-mid align-top">Tens of thousands of sites</td>
              <td class="p-4 text-text-mid align-top">Commercial and Commercial Plus</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="bg-white">
              <th scope="row" class="text-left p-4 font-semibold text-navy-dark align-top">Hospitality and fuel retail</th>
              <td class="p-4 text-text-mid align-top">Hundreds of EV-ready sites</td>
              <td class="p-4 text-text-mid align-top">Commercial Plus</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="bg-row-alt">
              <th scope="row" class="text-left p-4 font-semibold text-navy-dark align-top">EV fleet operators and charging hubs</th>
              <td class="p-4 text-text-mid align-top">Rapidly expanding fleets</td>
              <td class="p-4 text-text-mid align-top">Commercial Plus</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Founding team -->
  <section class="bg-paper">
    <div class="container-page section">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-10 lg:gap-16 items-center mb-12 md:mb-16">
        <div class="lg:col-span-7">
          <p class="eyebrow mb-3">The founding team</p>
          <h2 class="text-h2-sm md:text-h1 text-navy-dark">Three co-founders. Same workshop.</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-text-mid leading-relaxed">
            Precifarm was built by three Kenyan engineers who agreed that a solar installer that stays after the install needs to be designed that way from day one. We share a workshop, a hiring bar, and a five-year obligation to every customer.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="lg:col-span-5">
          <div class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-card shadow-xl ring-1 ring-black/5">
            <img
              src="/images/context/engineer-portrait.jpg"
              alt="A finished installation of black monocrystalline solar panels arranged across the tiled roof of a Kenyan home, with the rooftops of the surrounding neighbourhood and a hillside ridge visible in the background. Photographs like this one are what we mean when we talk about 'distributed solar': individual systems on individual buildings across the country, each one carrying the same engineering standard and the same five-year service commitment as the largest projects Precifarm operates."
              width="1600"
              height="1067"
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
              class="w-full h-full object-cover aspect-[4/3]"
            />
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        {team.map((member) => (
          <TeamCard
            name={member.name}
            role={member.role}
            bio={member.bio}
            verified={member.verified}
          />
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Six cities -->
  <section class="bg-white">
    <div class="container-page section">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mb-10 md:mb-12">
        <p class="eyebrow mb-3">Six cities, one team</p>
        <h2 class="text-h2-sm md:text-h1 text-navy-dark">Resident engineering, regional depots.</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-text-mid leading-relaxed">
          Nairobi headquarters plus five regional field hubs. Every installed system sits within a same-day drive of its regional depot.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-5">
        {cities.map((city) => (
          <CityCard city={city} />
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Operating principle prose -->
  <section class="bg-paper">
    <div class="container-page section">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-10 lg:gap-12">
        <div class="lg:col-span-1">
          <Callout variant="navy" eyebrow="The operating principle" asQuote={true}>
            {company.operatingPrinciple}
          </Callout>
        </div>
        <div class="lg:col-span-2 prose-precifarm">
          <p>
            Kenya's electrical infrastructure is becoming distributed. Households are stepping out from under unreliable grid supply. Schools and clinics are adopting solar because the grid alone is no longer a credible base-load promise. SMEs and cooperatives are sizing systems against productive loads they could never run before. EV operators are building charging mini-grids ahead of the curve. The country is wiring itself differently, and the contractors who carry that wiring forward will determine whether it stays running for the next decade.
          </p>
          <p>
            We started Precifarm because the contractor density Kenya needs has not yet been built. The country has plenty of installers; what it needs is operators. Engineering teams that show up after the install. Depots stocked in the regions where systems actually live. Five-year service commitments backed by the same hands that built the system. That is the gap we are filling.
          </p>
          <p>
            The workforce angle matters as much as the customer angle. Every additional Precifarm city is more Kenyan engineering jobs and more on-the-ground experience in regional energy infrastructure. We grow on revenue, not capital. We answer to the customers who pay our bills. We do the work that lets a Kenyan engineer point at a system she has serviced for five years and say it is still hers.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTASection
    variant="dark"
    headline="Send us your site. We will reply with a design."
    body="Two business days from your enquiry to a written design and quote. No commitment, no pressure."
    primaryCta={{ href: '/contact/', label: 'Get a quote' }}
    secondaryCta={{ href: '/how-we-work/', label: 'How we work' }}
  />
</BaseLayout>
